  "label": "Reconciliation gesture mapped onto dismissive text",
  "description": "The visual of two hands shaking (a gesture symbolizing reconciliation or agreement) is mapped onto the textual message 'let's shake hands and forget about that colonialism stuff.' This mapping creates an analogy where the handshake, typically a positive symbol of resolution, is contrasted with the text's call to ignore historical colonial injustices. The mapping highlights the irony or hypocrisy in using a gesture of unity to dismiss a deeply problematic historical legacy.",
